nEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"American (New), Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Food, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Food, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"D0AXNeHYbU9WfCBnbhYKXg","review_id":"XTfvROeTIdDunLLBkhRzmQ","date":"2019-12-23T22:45:30","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9214856028556824,"text_excerpt":"This is one of the vendors inside the refurbished St. Roch Market. Its basically an oyster bar but they have other offerings. This is an excellent place to grab a quick dozen raw for lunch or a snack, there are usually a range of oysters to choose from (local, Tx, Alabama etc). In my experiences here the oysters are properly shucked and I have not had a bad one. Also on the plus side, if your with a companion who is not a fan of the bi valve there are lots of other options including veggie things to eat here."},{"business_id":"D0AXNeHYbU9WfCBnbhYKXg","review_id":"cN9E69sbOxnkO3XG0p4nig","date":"2016-09-06T18:24:00","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.916449785232544,"text_excerpt":"We hung out at the St Roch Market twice and I also ate here twice. Both times were memorable. I had the Coconut Curry Gulf Shrimp, which was a steal for $9.00. I must say that I have been raving about this shrimp ever since. They were still in their shells, and the eyes and the antennae were still attached. I devoured these shrimp, shells and all. These shrimp were the sweetest, freshest most addicting shrimp I have ever eaten. Being from Philadelphia, the shrimp I buy or get at a restaurant is previously frozen. The shrimp at Elysian Seafood tasted like it had been caught that morning. The shrimp was served with a jasmine rice that had the flavors of jalopeno and cilantro running through..."},{"business_id":"D0AXNeHYbU9WfCBnbhYKXg","review_id":"COY8STW3qsA63t9irHCDcA","date":"2016-06-15T22:03:47","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9109554290771484,"text_excerpt":"Located at St. Roch Market (this market is becoming my favorite place to visit while vacationing in New Orleans), on the left hand side, next door to The Mayhaw Bar. My husband came here about 17 minutes before closing and took advantage of their happy hour special (Happy Hour: $0.75 oysters Sunday-Thursday 8-9 pm & Friday-Saturday 10-11 pm) and ordered 10 oysters ($7.50 + $0.75 tax= $8.25 total, prior to tip). The oysters (served raw), were delicious and fresh. This order came with cocktail sauce and a side of horseradish (neither of which I like to have with my raw oysters) and a few lemon wedges. We didn't wait too long for our oysters after making an order. But I just wished the sizin..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"D0AXNeHYbU9WfCBnbhYKXg","photo_id":"BaC6T-_wBzv0bLmehsNaMQ","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/BaC6T-_wBzv0bLmehsNaMQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9064383506774902},{"business_id":"D0AXNeHYbU9WfCBnbhYKXg","photo_id":"-CtVHYkynpi4rVDKqX9x1Q","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/-CtVHYkynpi4rVDKqX9x1Q.jpg","visual_representa